{
  "format": "register-decode/1",
  "description": "Raw words, in register-address order as read from the meter, and the decimal string each must decode to. Computed independently of either collector by contract/tools/register_decode.py (Python struct, decimal and fractions). Integers are the raw integer divided by 10^decimals, exactly, with decimals places. Floats have no decimals: each decodes to the shortest decimal that, parsed at the register's own width (f32 or f64, round half to even), gives back the same bits: the fewest significant digits (at most 9 for f32, 17 for f64), and of the decimals with that many digits that do, the nearest the float's exact value, a tie going to the even last digit. The f32 is never widened to f64 first. It is written out in full, with no exponent, no trailing zeros after the point and no trailing point; negative zero is -0. profiles: entries of contract/profiles, by profile, profile_version and register key. types: each data type and word order, for an entry given inline. no_value: words that must decode to no value at all, with the error. Every implementation that decodes registers must give every value and refuse every no_value. Changing an expected value changes what is billed.",
